      "writtenOn": "2021-07-02T17:53:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The bootImageConfig makes the assumption that the ArchType is unique per OsType. I think that is a reasonably safe assumption to make. I think everything would break if that was not true.\n\ne.g. the paths it creates only use OsType and ArchType to differentiate between the different image variants so if there was ever the case that multiple Android variants had the same ArchType then lots would break.\n\nSo, I don\u0027t think a panic here is particularly worth it.",
      "parentUuid": "77fc8b27_5f39c6aa",
